 "coverage_notes": {
  "adjudication": "Partly covered. Federal Register notices of hearings, applications, and licensing; SEC in-house proceedings; and FDA civil-money-penalty complaints on Regulations.gov. Not covered yet: NLRB Board and judges' decisions (the feed addresses still need confirming), and ALJ and appeals-board decisions at other agencies unless they appear in the Federal Register.",
  "enforcement": "Partly covered. Enforcement notices in the Federal Register and on Regulations.gov (since 2015); the SEC's litigation-release and administrative-proceeding feeds, and agency press feeds from the NLRB, FDA, and CFPB (recent items only); and FDA recall enforcement reports (since 2015). Not covered: FTC and FCC press releases (their websites refuse automated readers), EPA, DOL, FERC, and HHS-OIG enforcement announcements, and anything an agency never announces publicly.",
  "other": "Everything else the Federal Register publishes for the agency (meetings, information-collection requests, and similar notices) and routine Regulations.gov postings.",
  "presidential": "Well covered since 2015. Executive orders, memoranda, and proclamations published in the Federal Register. Presidential actions that are never published (for example, some directives and firings) are not.",
  "rulemaking": "Well covered since 2015. Proposed and final rules must be published in the Federal Register, which is checked for every tracked agency. Guidance and policy statements appear only if the agency published them there or on Regulations.gov."
 },
